              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Daniel 4:18",
        "book": "Daniel",
        "chapter": 4,
        "verse": 18
      },
      {
        "text": "Then Daniel, whose name was Belteshazzar, was astonied for one hour, and his thoughts troubled him. The king spake, and said, Belteshazzar, let not the dream, or the interpretation thereof, trouble thee. Belteshazzar answered and said, My lord, the dream be to them that hate thee, and the interpretation thereof to thine enemies.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 24,
            "end": 27
          },
          {
            "start": 255,
            "end": 257
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 19,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Daniel 4:19",
        "book": "Daniel",
        "chapter": 4,
        "verse": 19
      },
      {
        "text": "The tree that thou sawest, which grew, and was strong, whose height reached unto the heaven, and the sight thereof to all the earth;",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 20,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Daniel 4:20",
        "book": "Daniel",
        "chapter": 4,
        "verse": 20
      },
      {
        "text": "Whose leaves were fair, and the fruit thereof much, and in it was meat for all; under which the beasts of the field dwelt, and upon whose branches the fowls of the heaven had their habitation:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 13,
            "end": 17
          },
          {
            "start": 62,
            "end": 65
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 21,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Daniel 4:21",
        "book": "Daniel",
        "chapter": 4,
        "verse": 21
      },
      {
        "text": "It is thou, O king, that art grown and become strong: for thy greatness is grown, and reacheth unto heaven, and thy dominion to the end of the earth.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 116,
            "end": 124,
            "text": "Jer. 27:7 (6–8)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 3,
            "end": 5
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 22,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Daniel 4:22",
        "book": "Daniel",
        "chapter": 4,
        "verse": 22
      },
      {
        "text": "And whereas the king saw a watcher and an holy one coming down from heaven, and saying, Hew the tree down, and destroy it; yet leave the stump of the roots thereof in the earth, even with a band of iron and brass, in the tender grass of the field; and let it be wet with the dew of heaven, and let his portion be with the beasts of the field, till seven times pass over him;",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 294,
            "end": 297
          },
          {
            "start": 310,
            "end": 312
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 23,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Daniel 4:23",
        "book": "Daniel",
        "chapter": 4,
        "verse": 23
      },
      {
        "text": "This is the interpretation, O king, and this is the decree of the most High, which is come upon my lord the king:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 5,
            "end": 7
          },
          {
            "start": 45,
            "end": 47
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 24,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Daniel 4:24",
        "book": "Daniel",
        "chapter": 4,
        "verse": 24
      },
      {
        "text": "That they shall drive thee from men, and thy dwelling shall be with the beasts of the field, and they shall make thee to eat grass as oxen, and they shall wet thee with the dew of heaven, and seven times shall pass over thee, till thou know that the most High ruleth in the kingdom of men, and giveth it to whomsoever he will.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 25,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Daniel 4:25",
        "book": "Daniel",
        "chapter": 4,
        "verse": 25
      },
      {
        "text": "And whereas they commanded to leave the stump of the tree roots; thy kingdom shall be sure unto thee, after that thou shalt have known that the heavens do rule.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 26,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Daniel 4:26",
        "book": "Daniel",
        "chapter": 4,
        "verse": 26
      },
      {
        "text": "Wherefore, O king, let my counsel be acceptable unto thee, and break off thy sins by righteousness, and thine iniquities by shewing mercy to the poor; if it may be a lengthening of thy tranquillity.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 132,
            "end": 137,
            "text": "Mosiah 4:21 (16–21); D&C 42:31 (30–39)."
          },
          {
            "start": 151,
            "end": 153,
            "text": "OR so that your prosperity may be long."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 27,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Daniel 4:27",
        "book": "Daniel",
        "chapter": 4,
        "verse": 27
      },
      {
        "text": "All this came upon the king Nebuchadnezzar.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 28,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Daniel 4:28",
        "book": "Daniel",
        "chapter": 4,
        "verse": 28
      },
      {
        "text": "At the end of twelve months he walked in the palace of the kingdom of Babylon.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 29,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Daniel 4:29",
        "book": "Daniel",
        "chapter": 4,
        "verse": 29
      },
      {
        "text": "The king spake, and said, Is not this great Babylon, that I have built for the house of the kingdom by the might of my power, and for the honour of my majesty?",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 71,
            "end": 74,
            "text": "OR as a royal residence."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 30,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Daniel 4:30",
        "book": "Daniel",
        "chapter": 4,
        "verse": 30
      },
      {
        "text": "While the word was in the king’s mouth, there fell a voice from heaven, saying, O king Nebuchadnezzar, to thee it is spoken; The kingdom is departed from thee.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 140,
            "end": 148,
            "text": "Dan. 5:20."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 15,
            "end": 18
          },
          {
            "start": 72,
            "end": 79
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 31,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Dan. 5:20.",
            "prettyString": "Daniel 5:20",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "daniel",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 5,
                    "end": 5,
