                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Daniel 4:31",
        "book": "Daniel",
        "chapter": 4,
        "verse": 31
      },
      {
        "text": "And they shall drive thee from men, and thy dwelling shall be with the beasts of the field: they shall make thee to eat grass as oxen, and seven times shall pass over thee, until thou know that the most High ruleth in the kingdom of men, and giveth it to whomsoever he will.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 53,
            "end": 61
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 32,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Daniel 4:32",
        "book": "Daniel",
        "chapter": 4,
        "verse": 32
      },
      {
        "text": "The same hour was the thing fulfilled upon Nebuchadnezzar: and he was driven from men, and did eat grass as oxen, and his body was wet with the dew of heaven, till his hairs were grown like eagles’ feathers, and his nails like birds’ claws.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 198,
            "end": 207
          },
          {
            "start": 234,
            "end": 240
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 33,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Daniel 4:33",
        "book": "Daniel",
        "chapter": 4,
        "verse": 33
      },
      {
        "text": "And at the end of the days I Nebuchadnezzar lifted up mine eyes unto heaven, and mine understanding returned unto me, and I blessed the most High, and I praised and honoured him that liveth for ever, whose dominion is an everlasting dominion, and his kingdom is from generation to generation:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 18,
            "end": 26,
            "text": "IE the seven years."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 215,
            "end": 217
          },
          {
            "start": 259,
            "end": 261
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 34,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Daniel 4:34",
        "book": "Daniel",
        "chapter": 4,
        "verse": 34
      },
      {
        "text": "And all the inhabitants of the earth are reputed as nothing: and he doeth according to his will in the army of heaven, and among the inhabitants of the earth: and none can stay his hand, or say unto him, What doest thou?",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 52,
            "end": 59,
            "text": "Ps. 39:5; Isa. 40:15; Hel. 12:7; Moses 1:10."
          },
          {
            "start": 91,
            "end": 95,
            "text": "TG God, Will of."
          },
          {
            "start": 172,
            "end": 176,
